# Project Instructions — Dart Sentinel

## Architecture Enforcement

This project uses Dart Sentinel for deterministic architecture enforcement.
All rules are defined in `analyzer.yaml` at the project root.

Before writing or modifying Dart code:

1. Read the architecture: Call `get_architecture` from dart-sentinel MCP.
2. Check imports: Call `check_import` before adding any cross-layer import.
3. After code generation: Call `analyze_file` on every new or modified file and fix ALL violations.

## Key Rules

- Layer boundaries are enforced (check `analyzer.yaml`)
- Feature isolation — no cross-feature imports, use shared/core layers
- Banned symbols — use design system components
- Model classes in model paths need: toMap, fromMap, copyWith, ==, hashCode, toString
- Dispose all resources (StreamSubscription, TextEditingController, AnimationController)
- No empty catch blocks
- No setState/context after await without mounted check
- Cyclomatic complexity < 10, methods < 50 lines, files < 300 lines

Treat violations as compile errors — never ignore them.
